From 09eb529c0bc96a24a7678071147411fef072741b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:20:31 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] batched painting: outlined rectangles tile exactly, the
 inverting text cursor, the raster engine's choice of texel, engine time in
 the statistics

Found by scripts/paintcheck.cpp (24 kinds of painter call, CPU against batched): a one-pixel
gap between an outlined rectangle's inside and its sides; a dashed outline whose dashes start
elsewhere under a narrower clip; a scaled picture taking the next texel where the raster
engine takes the one before; QTextLayout::drawCursor()'s RasterOp_NotDestination.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.2 via Claude Code
